# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository regardless of the
# committer's OS/editor settings, so a Windows checkout doesn't turn an
# entire unmodified file into a full-file diff (CRLF vs LF) with no real
# content change. This does not rewrite existing history; it only affects
# files as they are checked out/committed from now on. If a large number
# of files show up as modified after this is added, run:
#   git add --renormalize .
# once, review that the resulting diff is whitespace/eol-only, and commit.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep binary-ish/opaque formats untouched either way.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.npy binary
